	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Off the southern coast of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn Vale{/link}, where for generations the charts have shown only open water, an island has come back out of the sea. On it stand the ruins of a troll city: paved squares, broad stairways, carved serpents and great stone heads, all crusted with coral. The waves swallowed it long ago. Now it has risen again, and it has not risen empty. {link:trolls}Trolls{/link} who should be long dead walk its terraces, the {link:naga}Naga{/link} have claimed its flooded halls, and a pirate ship lies broken among its stones.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The trolls of the jungle remember the city by the name of I'lalai. It was one of the cities of the old Gurubashi lands, which once stretched down to the sea. Its story is carved on four stone tablets. Their titles speak of a fate written in blood, of the first Tidebearer, of something cracked and cursed, and of a loa of the lost. What those words tell in full, few living scholars have yet read.

No chronicle records when I'lalai went under, or why. The coast has swallowed troll cities before. {link:kin-weelay}Kin'weelay{/link} of the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear Trolls{/link}, at {link:grom-gol-base-camp}Grom'gol Base Camp{/link}, tells how a great shudder of the earth once sank an old city beneath the waters of the Savage Coast, where murlocs now nest in its ruins. Whether I'lalai fell in the same way, and why it has now returned, no one has said.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:kin-weelay}Kin'weelay{/link} has set the tale of the tablets down in modern Zandali, and {link:loremaster-dibbs}Loremaster Dibbs{/link} has put it into the common tongue. The scholars' work has drawn attention to the ruins, but reaching them is another matter. No ship sails there. Part of the city still lies beneath the waves, in drowned halls the explorers call Atal'Byzal. A cave on the island, Sunken Hollow, holds a shimmering way into the depths of the city.

Within, the powers of the place pull against one another. The troll relics that the {link:naga}naga{/link} seers carry hum with a voodoo that seems to strain against the other magics of the city.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Those Who Dwell Here",
			text = [=[• {b}{link:zul-alai}Zul'Alai{/link}{/b}, a troll who has not stayed dead.
• {b}{link:var-taka}Var'Taka{/link}{/b} and {b}{link:zin-aka}Zin'aka{/link}{/b}, whose names are those of trolls.
• {b}{link:captain-dreadrise}Captain Dreadrise{/link}{/b}, whose ship may be the wreck among the ruins.
• {b}{link:deathless-marrow}Deathless Marrow{/link}{/b}, a power of the elements, with a primeval elemental at its side.
• {b}{link:gill}Gill{/link}{/b}, a lesser elemental.
• {b}{link:min-loth-the-serpent}Min'loth the Serpent{/link}{/b}, whose title speaks of the sea.
• The {link:naga}naga{/link} of the Brinescale, Saltscale and Saltseer, the deathless sorcerers, and the makrura and crabs of the shallows.]=],
		},
